# `@cmolg/*` packages resolve from Javadaba's PRIVATE registry (GitHub Packages),
# NOT the public npm registry.
#
# `@cmolg/daba-engine` is closed-source (see, in the javadaba-web Core,
# docs/adr/0003-daba-engine-cerrado-registro-privado.md): only the compiled
# `dist/` + type declarations are published, never the TypeScript source. The
# source lives solely in `../javadaba-web/packages/daba-engine`.
#
# ── WHY THE SCOPE IS `@cmolg` AND NOT `@javadaba` ────────────────────────────
# GitHub Packages requires the npm scope to match the login of the account that
# owns the repository. The Core lives in `CMolG/javadaba-webpage`, so publishing
# `@javadaba/*` answered `403 permission_denied: create_package` — no token could
# fix that. The `javadaba` login has been taken since 2011 by an unrelated third
# party, and on GitHub users and organisations share one namespace, so an org
# with that name could not be created either.
#
# The user's decision (2026-08-07) — this split IS the new coherence:
#   · PRIVATE -> scope `@cmolg`    on GitHub Packages  (this engine)
#   · PUBLIC  -> scope `@javadaba` on public npm       (e.g. `@javadaba/seo-sdk`)
#
# ── ⚠️ THIS IS A PUBLIC REPO DEPENDING ON A PRIVATE PACKAGE ──────────────────
# heliox-ide is Apache-2.0 and public; `@cmolg/daba-engine` is proprietary and
# private. **Anyone who clones this repo without registry access CANNOT run
# `npm install`** — it will fail resolving the engine. That is the accepted
# trade-off of ADR 0003 (closed engine, open Fluxor), not an accident. Options
# for contributors are in that ADR: a read token for trusted collaborators, or a
# public stub of the engine's interface for a degraded build.
#
# ── THE TOKEN ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `npm install` needs a token with the `read:packages` scope exported as
# NODE_AUTH_TOKEN in the environment. It is injected by ENVIRONMENT and never
# committed: the line below is a REFERENCE to the variable, never a value.
@cmolg:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com
//npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=${NODE_AUTH_TOKEN}
